foundation.question_text:
A square courtyard has area $576$ m$^{2}$, and $576=2^{6}\times 3^{2}$.
Find the side length of the courtyard.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3.0,3.0);
\node at (1.5,1.5) {$576\text{ m}^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.solution_text:
Halve each index.
$\sqrt{576}=2^{3}\times 3$
$=8\times 3$
$=24$
The side length is $24$ m.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3.0,3.0);
\node at (1.5,1.5) {$576\text{ m}^{2}$};
\node[below] at (1.5,0) {$24\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,1.5) {$24\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

