development.question_text:
A square mosaic is made from $1764$ square tiles, and $1764=2^{2}\times 3^{2}\times 7^{2}$.
How many tiles lie along each edge?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3.0,3.0);
\node at (1.5,1.5) {$1764\text{ tiles}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.solution_text:
Halve each index.
$\sqrt{1764}=2\times 3\times 7$
$=42$
There are $42$ tiles along each edge.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3.0,3.0);
\node at (1.5,1.5) {$1764\text{ tiles}$};
\node[below] at (1.5,0) {$42$};
\node[left] at (0,1.5) {$42$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
